  "scope": "Unchanged NPCDropTables (drop, createDrop, getLooter, sendDropMessage, handleBoneCrusher), GroundItemManager, GroundItem, DeathTask, NodeTask, Pulse, PulseManager, PulseType, Bones and the table classes of the roll on JDK 11; PulseRunner with one added import alias for its clock. Original text inserted at generation time: Entity commenceDeath/finalizeDeath/startDeath; NPC tick, onRespawn, finalizeDeath, commenceDeath, handleDrops, getAudio, getDropLocation and the respawn accessors; ImpactHandler getMostDamageEntity, its log and disabled-tick accessors, and the two parts of handleImpact that write the logs and start a death; RegionChunk.add(GroundItem); Item and ItemDefinition accessors; Definition.getConfiguration; announceIfRare; Location.getDistance; StringUtils.getFormattedNumber. Recording adapters: every other Entity, NPC and Player member, the behaviour, zone monitor, clan and loot-share state, Grand Exchange price, item plugins, skills, messages, news, statistics, bots, packets, the chunk lookup and the list of local and online players. Item definitions, NPC configuration values, entity hash codes and the tick driver (pulses, then NPC ticks) are case inputs. The roll is seeded as in the drop-table oracle; no shared table or clue is loaded. Not exercised: DeathTask.getContainers, a dying player's own commenceDeath/finalizeDeath, the rest of handleImpact, ground-item removal and expiry, packet bytes, NPC.clear.",
